## Write 64 as a power of 4
64 &= 4 \times 4 \times 4
&= 4^3
## Write 1/16 as a power of 4
16 &= 4^2
\frac{1}{16} &= \frac{1}{4^2}
Use $\frac{1}{a^n} = a^{-n}$.
&= 4^{-2}
## Write 2 as a power of 4
$2 = \sqrt{4}$, and a square root is the power $\tfrac{1}{2}$.
2 &= \sqrt{4}
&= 4^{1/2}
ANSWER: 64 = 4^{3},\ \ \frac{1}{16} = 4^{-2},\ \ 2 = 4^{1/2}

## Substitute x = 11
F(11) &= 440 \times 2^{\frac{11}{12}}
&= 830.6\ldots
&\approx 831
ANSWER: 831 \text{ Hz}

## Use F(-x) for a note below Concert A
A note 6 notes below uses $x = -6$.
F(-6) &= 440 \times 2^{-\frac{6}{12}}
## Simplify the power
&= 440 \times 2^{-\frac{1}{2}}
&= \frac{440}{\sqrt{2}}
## Evaluate and round to 4 significant figures
&= 311.126\ldots
&\approx 311.1
ANSWER: 311.1 \text{ Hz}

## Differentiate the exponential
Use $\frac{d}{dx}\left(a^{kx}\right) = k\ln a \cdot a^{kx}$ with $a = 2$ and $k = \frac{1}{12}$.
F(x) &= 440 \times 2^{\frac{x}{12}}
F'(x) &= 440 \times 2^{\frac{x}{12}} \times \ln 2 \times \frac{1}{12}
&= \frac{110\ln 2}{3} \times 2^{\frac{x}{12}}
ANSWER: F'(x) = 440 \times 2^{\frac{x}{12}} \times \ln 2 \times \frac{1}{12}

## Epley formula with r = 5
M_E &= w\left(1 + \frac{5}{30}\right)
&= w \times \frac{35}{30}
&= \frac{7w}{6}
## Brzycki formula with r = 5
M_B &= w\left(\frac{36}{37 - 5}\right)
&= w \times \frac{36}{32}
&= \frac{9w}{8}
## Subtract using a common denominator
M_B - M_E &= \frac{9w}{8} - \frac{7w}{6}
&= \frac{27w}{24} - \frac{28w}{24}
&= -\frac{w}{24}
## State the difference
The difference is the size of this value.
\text{Difference} &= \frac{w}{24}
ANSWER: \frac{w}{24}
